======================================================================
APPENDIX — TARGET ARCHITECTURE
======================================================================
Principles
- Source of truth for artifacts is the spec; for orchestration it is the runner's state and verdict files.
- Separation of duties: nothing grades its own work; verifiers never fix; verifiers never write artifacts, traces or verdicts; generators never author the evidence they are judged on.
- Orchestration, trace extraction, structural checks, scoring, state and file writes are DETERMINISTIC CODE. Claude does generation and semantic judgement only; its output is always data, never control.
- A `pass` is auto-approved for merge; therefore the scorer must be unarguable and the audit log complete.
- Verification is automatic: gates run immediately after their generator, never by manual invocation; humans may force or stop.
- Multi-day, human-in-the-loop, resumable, interruptible.
- Seamless for the client: same commands, same artifacts, staged modes, reversible.

Chain of trust
  PRD ──(semantic council)──▶ spec ──(extract_traces.py)──▶ expected traces
                                                  │
                        BPMN / tasks / Java checked against ◀┘

Commands (final set; existing names unchanged)
  opsx:propose-intent        PRD → spec + BPMN
  opsx:propose-design        thin wrapper → runner --phase design. Two nodes, same design-author agent:
                             propose_design_clarify (--steps 1-3) and propose_design_build (--steps 4-7,
                             requires_verdict gate_design == pass). Runner picks entry node from state; user
                             always types the same command. State between halves is carried only via artifacts on disk.
  opsx:verify-semantic-design / opsx:verify-semantic-author   juror agents
  opsx:verify-structural-design / opsx:verify-structural-author   deterministic scripts
  opsx:verify-design         single read-only agent, proposal/design/tasks vs spec + BPMN + traces
  opsx:apply / opsx:verify   stock OpenSpec, unchanged
  opsx:score <phase>         deterministic scorer
  opsx:gate <phase>          runs council + structural in parallel, scorer, writes verdict; phases: design | design_artifacts | author
  opsx:run                   thin wrapper → runner

Rules
- Expected traces come from the spec only via extract_traces.py → .openspec/<change>/traces/. BPMN and Java are never a source of traces. Only extract_traces.py writes traces/.
- verify-structural-design: every expected trace realizable in BPMN; BPMN well-formed; orphan BPMN paths flagged.
- verify-structural-author: traces vs Java structure derived from control flow / call graph; annotations are hints only; original BPMN is a secondary cross-check; a juror checks each annotation's claim matches the code beneath it.
- Structural never consumes semantic output. Both feed the scorer only.
- Council: 3 independent jurors, same inputs, parallel, no cross-visibility, lenses coverage / invariants & edge cases / adversarial, vary model where possible, identical strict-JSON output (per-requirement 0–1, findings, overall), tools Read/Glob/Grep only, maxTurns capped. Jurors return JSON in final message; runner writes files. verify-design gate uses a single juror.
- Scorer: pure function of (juror JSON, structural JSON, config) → pass | fail | human_review with reason. Per-requirement median; any spread > disagreement_max → human_review; loops > max_loops → human_review.
- Verdict files hash inputs; requires_verdict refuses stale inputs.

Config (adapt to my existing schema; additive)
  orchestration.mode: manual | observed | assisted | driven
     manual = today; observed = wrapped commands record state and run gates in shadow, bootstraps in-flight changes;
     assisted = commands consult state, run gates and inject feedback before continuing, human still sequences phases;
     driven = runner advances to checkpoints (--step default, --auto).
     Manual invocation stays valid in every mode and is implemented as runner --from <node> --until <next checkpoint>, logged by: human.
  gates.<phase>.strictness: shadow | advisory | enforced   (shadow = write verdict, never block; advisory = show, user decides; enforced = loop/block/auto-approve)
  scorer.design:  { pass: {semantic_min: 0.85, per_req_min: 0.7, structural: pass}, fail: {structural: fail}, else: human_review }
  scorer.author:  { pass: {semantic_min: 0.90, per_req_min: 0.8, invariants_all_met: true, structural: pass}, fail: {structural: fail}, else: human_review }
  scorer.max_loops: 3
  council: { size: 3, aggregate: median, disagreement_max: 0.25, on_disagreement: human_review }
  notify: { command: null }

State & files (all under .openspec/<change>/, plain text, committable, lock file)
  state.yaml       current node, completed nodes {in_hash, out_hash, ts, by}, loop counters, awaiting, mode, migrated flag
  traces/          spec-derived trace tables
  verdicts/<phase>-<n>.yaml   immutable; inputs hashes, jurors[{id, lens, model, per_requirement, overall, findings}],
                   aggregate, structural{result, missing_traces, orphan_paths, findings}, verdict, reason, decided_by
  human/           clarifications.md + .answers.yaml; <phase>-<n>.decision.yaml {decision: approve|reject|reset_loops, reason, by, ts}
  runs/*.jsonl     append-only audit log

Agents (.claude/agents/)
  intent-author, design-author: Read, Write, Edit, Glob, Grep
  implementer: all tools
  semantic-{design,author}-juror-{coverage,invariants,adversarial}, design-verifier: Read, Glob, Grep; maxTurns
  Verifiers receive only artifacts as input, never generator conversation. Different framing/model for verifiers vs authors.

Hooks
  PreToolUse Write|Edit: block proposal/design/tasks writes without a pass verdict with matching hashes (enforced mode only)
  PreToolUse Write|Edit: block verdicts/** unless caller is runner; block traces/** unless caller is extract_traces.py
  Stop/SubagentStop on author agents: record state and invoke runner --gate-only for the current phase
  PostToolUse Write|Edit on spec/BPMN/src: mark state dirty so next run re-gates first

Runner (scripts/run_pipeline.py + .openspec/pipeline.yaml)
  Node types: agent | gate | checkpoint | human_input | human_review | terminal. Fields: inputs, outputs, requires_verdict, feedback_from, loop_counter, on:{pass,fail,human_review}, next.
  Only the runner chooses the next node, solely from verdict enums in files it wrote.
  Idempotent nodes keyed by input sha256; --resume is default; --restart explicit; --status; --from; --until; --dry-run; --pause-after.
  Gates: pre scripts → council + structural in parallel → one retry on invalid juror JSON then human_review → scorer → atomic verdict write → transition.
  Checkpoints after each pass: snapshot hashes, record git SHA only if committed, commit: optional|required|auto (default optional), stop with exit 3 unless --auto.
  Human nodes: write questions / wait for decision file; exit 3 WAITING_FOR_HUMAN; resume when schema-valid file exists.
  Human control: --gate-only [--phase]; --force; --from; --override <gate> --decision --reason (decision file, verdict immutable); --stop flag file; SIGINT/SIGTERM → terminate children, state `interrupted` at node boundary; interrupted gate/generator re-runs from scratch on resume; checkpointed phases never redo.
  Infra failures (crash, missing outputs, bad JSON) → exit 2, never a fail verdict. Exit codes: 0 done, 2 infra halt, 3 waiting for human.
  Stale detection on every resume: re-hash inputs of current node and requires_verdict deps; on mismatch stop and name the earliest node to re-run from.
  Notify hook on WAITING_FOR_HUMAN, human_review, merge_ready, infra halt.

Migration constraints
- Preserve every command name, argument and artifact path. New commands additive. Deprecated commands print a notice and delegate.
- Schema changes additive with defaults; existing specs still validate; trace extraction warns, not fails, on unstructured requirements until enforced.
- Default after implementation: orchestration.mode observed, all gates shadow. Rollout per gate, design first, author last, promoted on eval evidence.
- Bootstrap state for in-flight changes from existing artifacts, marked migrated: true; never require restarting a change.
- Rollback: mode manual; all new state is confined to .openspec/<change>/ and removable without touching artifacts.
